<title>ISRAEL: Israel Feb economic performance index up 0.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Israel Feb economic performance index up 0.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's economic performance or &quot;S&quot; index rose 0.8 percent in February after declining three months in a row, the Bank of Israel said.</p>
<p>				Feb 97    Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p>Month-on-month change   + 0.8     - 0.1     + 1.2</p>
<p>Index (base 100=1994)   117.3     116.4     115.4</p>
<p>The &quot;S&quot; index is made up of three components: retail sales, which fell 1.1 percent in Febuary; imports, which fell 1.8 percent in February; and industrial production, which rose 1.2 percent in January.</p>
<p>Note: figures for industrial production lag.</p>
<p>- Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-537-502</p>
</text>
